# The world of the halti tasks, for a task's setup to source in its empty work dir: a git repository standing for
# a Mac clone of a client's `payments` service, halti's config folder under the run's HOME (three workspaces: crewpoint,
# a client's, open with its box running; research, a client's, open and stopped; emanative, the user's own, closed),
# and the stand-in halti's state (box contents under box/, door logs). The setup then adds its own files and calls seed.
set -eu
EVAL_HOME=${EVAL_HOME:-$HOME}
S=${HALTI_FAKE_STATE:-$EVAL_HOME/.halti-fake}
put() { mkdir -p "$(dirname "$1")" && cat >"$1"; }
# seed: the stand-in approves the rules as they are now (the user's last approval).
seed() { PATH=/usr/bin:/bin "$EVAL_LIB/halti" --fake-init; }
put "README.md" <<'EOF'
# payments

Crewpoint's payments service (client work). This is the Mac clone; agents work on it in the
crewpoint workspace's box (halti), where it is the payments folder under /work.
EOF
